  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: All for One and One for All Poker. Flow: ante, deal five down, opening bet, repeated draw+bet loops, showdown. Draw choices are exactly 0, 1, or 5; enforce stock-safety rule on 5-card exchanges.',
    Player: 'Welcome to All for One. You start with 5 cards. In each draw round you may exchange all five, exchange one, or stand pat. Every draw round is followed by betting, and once the stock gets too short for another draw cycle the game goes to showdown.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the best 5-card poker hand at showdown or by forcing all other players to fold.',
    gameplay: '1. **Initial Deal**: 5 cards each. Initial betting round. 2. **Repeated Draw Phases**: Each active player must choose one of three options: \n   - **All for One**: Discard your entire 5-card hand and draw 5 new ones.\n   - **One for All**: Discard exactly 1 card and draw 1 new one.\n   - **Stand Pat**: Keep your current hand (once you stand pat, you cannot draw in future rounds).\n3. **Betting**: Each draw phase is followed by a full betting round. 4. **Repetition**: Draw and betting rounds continue until the deck has too few cards left to fulfill a worst-case draw scenario (i.e., every participant drawing 5). 5. **Showdown**: Remaining players reveal hands. Best hand according to standard rankings wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'No half-measures: You cannot discard 2, 3, or 4 cards. It is strictly 1 or 5 or 0.',
      'Standing Pat: Once a player stands pat, they are locked into that hand for the remainder of the deal.',
      'End Condition: The game ends automatically when the deck contains fewer than (Active Players * 5) cards, or by mutual agreement if betting becomes circular.',
    ],
